2
00:12:16,363 --> 00:12:22,363
The Outlaw Josey Wales is a western film directed by Clint Eastwood.

3
00:18:24,545 --> 00:18:30,545
After avenging his family's brutal murder, Wales
is pursued by a pack of soldiers.

4
00:24:32,727 --> 00:24:38,727
He prefers to travel alone, but ragtag outcasts are drawn to him - and
Wales can't bring himself to leave them unprotected.

5
00:30:40,909 --> 00:30:46,909
Josey Wales, played by Clint Eastwood.

6
00:36:49,090 --> 00:36:55,090
Lone Watie, played by Chief Dan George.

7
00:42:57,272 --> 00:43:03,272
Laura Lee, played by Sondra Locke.

8
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Terrill, played by Bill McKinney.

9
00:55:13,636 --> 00:55:19,636
Fletcher, played by John Vernon.

10
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
Grandma Sarah, played by Paula Trueman.

11
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The Outlaw Josey Wales is a 1976 American revisionist Western
film set during and after the American Civil War.

12
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
It was directed by and starred Clint Eastwood (as Josey Wales), with Chief
Dan George, Sondra Locke, Bill McKinney, and John Vernon.

13
01:19:46,363 --> 01:19:52,363
During the Civil War, Josey Wales is a Missouri farmer turned soldier, who seeks to
avenge the death of his family and gains a reputation as a feared gunfighter.

14
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
At the end of the war, his group surrenders, but is massacred, and Wales
becomes an outlaw, pursued by bounty hunters and soldiers.

15
01:32:02,727 --> 01:32:08,727
The film was adapted by Sonia Chernus and Philip Kaufman from author Asa Earl "Forrest" Carter's 1972 novel The
Rebel Outlaw: Josey Wales (republished, as shown in the movie's opening credits, as Gone to Texas).

16
01:38:10,909 --> 01:38:16,909
The film was a commercial success, earning $31.8
million against a $3.7 million budget.

17
01:44:19,090 --> 01:44:25,090
In 1996, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

18
01:50:27,272 --> 01:50:33,272
Josey Wales was portrayed by Michael Parks in the film's
1986 sequel, The Return of Josey Wales.

19
01:56:35,454 --> 01:56:41,454
His wife Laura Lee was played by Mary Ann Averett in the sequel.

20
02:02:43,636 --> 02:02:49,636
The film explores themes of showdown, loss of loved
one, texas, settler, native american.

21
02:08:51,818 --> 02:08:57,818
The tone is dark.
